# Cloudflare Pages response headers for the static site (R6-S1 / S2).
#
# The CSP is the third leg of the reflected-XSS fix (the other two — numeric coercion + URL
# scheme-validation at every sink in index.html, and dev-gating the ?api/?stub/?worker overrides in
# assets/core.js — each independently break the exploit chain; this blunts anything missed and adds
# clickjacking + exfil defence).
#
# Honest tradeoff: index.html and how-it-works.html each ship one large INLINE <script>, and a Pages
# _headers file is static (no per-response nonce), so script-src must carry 'unsafe-inline' — which
# does NOT by itself block an injected inline onerror. It DOES lock external/eval script, restrict
# fetch/XHR to the two configured backends (blocking evil-backend exfil and reinforcing the override
# gate), pin img to poecdn, and deny framing. connect-src lists exactly the API + worker from
# config.js PLUS cloudflareinsights.com (the Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon — cookieless, aggregate
# page-views only; static.cloudflareinsights.com is allowed in script-src, disclosed on how-it-works).
# img-src is poecdn only (the site uses zero data: images — verified). To later drop 'unsafe-inline'
# from script-src, move both inline <script> blocks into /assets/*.js (mechanical).

/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://static.cloudflareinsights.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https://web.poecdn.com; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://divtally.vercel.app https://divtally-cache.divtally.workers.dev https://cloudflareinsights.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
